{
    "map": {
        "description": "Adds a diagram rule to a diagram template to set diagram features currently represented in the diagram as starting points for tracing rules. The diagram features are queried from a given network source class or object table and can be filtered by their attributes.",
        "description.descr": "The description of the rule.",
        "description.title": "Description",
        "in_utility_network.descr": "The utility network or trace network containing the diagram template that will be modified.",
        "in_utility_network.title": "Input Network",
        "is_active.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the rule will be active when generating and updating diagrams based on the specified template.<ul><li>Checked—The added rule will become active during the generation and update of any diagrams based on the input template. This is the default.</li><li>Unchecked—The added rule will not become active during the generation or update of any diagrams based on the input template.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "is_active.title": "Active",
        "junction_terminals.descr": "<xdoc><p>The terminal IDs that will start tracing if the network source class or object table references network junctions with terminals.</p><p>All the terminal IDs retrieved for the junctions in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Network Source</span> parameter are listed. They correspond to those in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Terminal Configurations</span> section on the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Network Properties</span> tab.</p><p>When both the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Expression</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Junction Terminal(s)</span> parameters are configured, the specified terminals must correspond to queried features or objects; otherwise, no starting points will be set.</p></xdoc>",
        "junction_terminals.title": "Junction Terminal(s)",
        "network_source.descr": "The network source class or object table that references the features or objects that will be set as starting points.",
        "network_source.title": "Network Source",
        "out_template_name.title": "Output Diagram Template",
        "out_utility_network.title": "Output Network",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Adds a diagram rule to a diagram template to set diagram features currently represented in the diagram as starting points for tracing rules. The diagram features are queried from a given network source class or object table and can be filtered by their attributes.</p><note type=\"caution\"/><p group=\"note\">This tool is a configuration and administration tool.</p><note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">This tool impacts the consistency of any existing diagrams based on the input diagram template. All of the existing diagrams become inconsistent and open with a consistency warning icon until they are updated.</p></xdoc>",
        "template_name.descr": "The name of the diagram template that will be modified.",
        "template_name.title": "Input Diagram Template",
        "title": "Add Set Starting Point By Attribute Rule",
        "where_clause.descr": "An SQL expression to select the subset of features or objects in the specified source class or object table that will be set as starting points. For more information on SQL syntax, see SQL reference for query expressions used in ArcGIS.",
        "where_clause.title": "Expression"
    }
}
